    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0252" n="242" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg242"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/11–344: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-02T10:45:00-04:00">December 2,
                            1944—10:45 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–2536. For Schoenfeld (Czechoslovak Series No. —). Reference your despatch no.
                    207, November 3, 1944.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d189-f1"/> Department does not
                    believe international conference on subject of looting and flight of Axis
                    capital would be profitable at this time. Subject of restitution continues to be
                    explored, and is being discussed with Robbins of the AmEmbassy London. Work is
                    going forward on flight of Axis capital problems, on the operating and policy
                    levels, and it would appear that nothing would be gained by international
                    conference discussion of the subject, at least at this stage. The interest of
                    the Czechoslovak Government, and of other governments in similar positions, is
                    realized, and their cooperation on these subjects, where their interest is
                    clear, will be sought.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
